<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#coffee-economy">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coffee economy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as coffee</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Coffee is a drink made from the roasted seeds of the coffee plant, originally from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, which spread through the Islamic world and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Coffee became the dominant export of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>, cultivated by enslaved labour, and a plantation crop in French colonies. It was also traded through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>'s coffee houses were centres of intellectual life in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>.</p></div>
